\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{One elimination or two}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{A [residual Wick evaluation](fdip-008N) returns a polynomial in the retained variables. The [gauge average](fdip-0083) of a bounded observable returns an invariant function. A [paired coefficient](fdip-00IX) can send the unit to zero and still return a determinant. Each of these operations lands in a smaller algebra. When does one elimination, specified on its own, equal the same elimination performed in two successive steps?}
